==English==
{{was wotd|2026|January|23}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=fare|*(s)twerH-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|perturben|t=to disturb (someone) mentally, disquiet; to cause disorder to (something), confuse; to hinder (something)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=perturben|pos=v|id=MED33142}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|perturber}}, and from its {{lg|etymon}} {{der|en|la|perturbāre}}, the {{lg|present}} {{lg|active}} {{lg|infinitive}} of {{m|la|perturbō|t=to confuse; to alarm, disturb, trouble, perturb}}, from {{m|la|per-|pos={{lg|intensifying}} {{lg|prefix}}}} + {{m|la|turbō|t=to agitate, disturb, unsettle, perturb; to upset}}<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=5304084336|date=March 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> (from {{m|la|turba|t=disorder, disturbance, turmoil}} (possibly from {{der|en|grc|τῠ́ρβη|t=confusion, disorder, tumult}}, either from {{der|en|qsb-grc}}, or {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)twerH-|t=to agitate, stir up; to urge on, propel}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos={{lg|suffix}} forming {{lg|infinitive}}s of regular first-{{lg|conjugation}} {{lg|verb}}s}}).

